## What I learned
- The repo contains exercises for the whole curriculum — only open the folder
  the current lesson tells you to (I got lost in advanced-html-css at first)
- Quote rules in font-family: quotes wrap ONE multi-word font name only,
  not the whole list: `Verdana, "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif`
- Every separator in a font list must be a comma — a missing comma kills
  the whole declaration silently
- `height: auto` + fixed width = image keeps its proportions
- Boilerplate meta tags: `X-UA-Compatible` is a fossil for dead IE;
  `viewport` makes pages render properly on phones (essential)
- VS Code: Ctrl+Shift+P = command palette (search any feature by name)

